%% ClearLedger application architecture
%% web/: React workspace bundled with esbuild and served by the Go API.
%% backend/: HTTP API, reconciliation domain, storage, agent, and event worker.
%% compose.yaml: PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, API, worker, and optional Ollama.
%% deploy/: optional Caddy reverse proxy and Cloudflare Tunnel configuration.
%% samples/: synthetic CSV inputs. scripts/: deployment acceptance check.
%% .github/workflows/: backend tests, static checks, frontend build, Compose validation.
%% Local mode uses JSON file storage and direct investigations, without outbox or worker.
%% PostgreSQL stores one bounded JSONB workspace aggregate and a transactional outbox.
%% Kafka delivery is at least once; application receipts make effects idempotent.
%% Agent drafts require human review and cannot execute financial actions.
flowchart TD
    UI[React workspace] --> API[Go HTTP API]
    CSV[Synthetic CSV samples or user imports] --> API
    API --> PG[(PostgreSQL workspace state and outbox)]
    API --> R[(Redis investigation rate limits)]
    API --> LOCAL[(JSON file in local mode)]
    PG --> O[Outbox relay]
    O --> K[Kafka reconciliation events]
    K --> W[Go investigation worker]
    W --> A[Bounded agent controller]
    API --> A
    A --> M[Optional local Ollama model]
    A --> E[Case evidence tools]
    W --> PG
    API --> REVIEW[Human review notes]
    REVIEW --> PG
